00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
okay in this video we're going to be

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.600
discussing how to find linear speed and

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.666
angular speed so a lot of times students

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.666
have questions about this concept how do

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.666
I find linear speed and angular speed it

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.600
seems like a real difficult concept but

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.133
really all it is is doing a unit

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.666
conversion or unit analysis type problem

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.310
so I'll show you an example so say for

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:03.870
example we want to find out what the

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:08.649
angular speed is for

00:00:08.649 --> 00:00:10.900
a wheel that's turning at 4 revolutions

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:11.980
per minute

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.750
okay so just a wheel that's rotating at

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.150
4 revolutions per minute so what you do

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:21.970
is you start off with 4 revolutions per

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:26.350
one minute okay and what you want to do

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:28.210
is you want to convert into the angular

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.640
speed so that's the angle per unit time

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:35.379
so what we're going to do is we're going

00:00:35.379 --> 00:00:42.580
to multiply by 2 pi radians per 1

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:45.459
revolution so if you remember unit

00:00:45.459 --> 00:00:48.370
circle 2 pi radians is what one

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:51.760
revolution is equivalent to and so your

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.370
revolutions cancel and now you have

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:57.070
radians per minute if you multiply the

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:02.309
numerators and denominators you get 8 pi

00:01:02.309 --> 00:01:09.090
radians per minute so that's your angle

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:12.220
per unit time your angular speed

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.290
now if you want to find your linear

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:17.500
speed say this wheel that we're

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.860
discussing let's just say it has a three

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:23.140
foot diameter so say this is three feet

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.080
and if we remember that circumference

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:29.080
equals pi times diameter so

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:30.430
circumference the distance all the way

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:32.620
around so the circumference is going to

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:38.410
be 3 pi feet for every one revolution so

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.809
you go once around that distance is 3 pi

00:01:40.809 --> 00:01:43.660
feet for every one turn where every one

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:46.300
rotation so if we want to convert from 4

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.100
revolutions per minute

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:51.280
to the linear speed linear[speed] is like the

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:55.470
length per unit time we've got four revs

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:59.950
per one minute and we're going to

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:03.450
multiply by for every one revolution

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:06.880
you're going to be traveling 3pi feet so

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:11.200
three PI feet so you can see that the

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.170
revolutions cancel and you end up with

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:17.620
feet per minute so let's just multiply

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:26.130
across that's 12 pi feet per one minute

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:30.430
okay so that's angular speed and linear

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:33.130
speed so the next problem I want to show

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.000
you this one's a little bit more

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.500
complicated some students have trouble

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.810
with this but again just think about

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.470
converting from the unit's that you

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.240
don't want into the unit's that you do

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.670
want so let's take a look at that

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:47.380
problem so what we're going to do in

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:49.570
this one we'll analyze a vehicle that's

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:54.070
traveling at 60 miles per hour okay some

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:56.470
type of a vehicle is traveling at 60

00:02:56.470 --> 00:03:02.080
miles per hour and let's just say that

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.750
the tires on this vehicle let's just say

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:10.060
that they're 1.5 feet okay that's the

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:11.770
diameter which means that the

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:16.990
circumference is 1.5 pi feet per one Rev

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:18.700
and let's say we want to convert to

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:22.060
revolutions per minute so we're starting

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.860
with 60 miles per hour the vehicles

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:27.520
traveling we're going to convert miles

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:28.360
into feet

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:33.670
so one mile for every 5,280 feet so see

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:35.259
how the miles cancel numerator and

00:03:35.259 --> 00:03:37.660
denominator so you end up with feet per

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:42.250
hour now the feet we know there's 1.5 PI

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:48.190
feet per revolution so let's convert 1.5

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:53.710
PI feet per 1 Rev so the feet cancels

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.420
the numerator denominator they cancel

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.480
now we have revolutions per hour we want

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:00.550
to convert that into

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:03.550
revolutions per minute okay so right now

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:09.010
we've got hours so let's see here we've

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:12.610
got for every one hour there are 60

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:15.760
minutes so you can see the hours are

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:17.980
cancelling with the hours denominator

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.990
and numerator and we're going to end up

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:21.700
with the units we do want which are

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:23.560
revolutions per minute

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:25.960
your revolutions per minute so all you

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.300
have to do is multiply across all the

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.380
numerators all the denominators and

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.970
divide so we'll just do that real quick

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:37.450
on the calculator so you have that if

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:43.600
you want to compare 60 times 5,280 okay

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:49.120
divided by in parentheses 1.5 pi times

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:52.660
60 so we get one thousand one hundred

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:56.860
and twenty point five so one thousand

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:59.310
one hundred and twenty point five

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:07.000
revolutions per minute so these are a

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.280
couple examples for finding linear speed

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:11.620
angular speed just think of it as a unit

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:15.550
conversion problem and that'll make it

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.680
simple to solve so check out some of my

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.300
other videos if you have other questions

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:21.100
regarding problems you're having with

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:25.420
your math and if you need to review this video again to understand

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:29.880
these problems better, see you in the next video

